course: dictionary
lesson: 6265
title: Same spelling, different meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some short words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «Mon» is a good example. Read the words around it before you decide what it means.
explain: In a timetable or diary, «Mon» is short for Monday. «Mon–Fri» means Monday to Friday, so Monday is the first day of the school week.
explain: In a story from the Caribbean, a friend says, «Yeah, mon!» Here mon is a friendly word for "man", used when talking to a friend. In Scotland, a fan shouts, «Mon the team!» That is a cheer that means "come on, team!"
explain: Ask yourself what kind of text you are reading: a diary, a story or a football match. Then choose the meaning that fits, and check it by putting it into the sentence.
fact: «Mon» is the short form of Monday, used in timetables and calendars.
fact: «Mon–Fri» means Monday to Friday.
fact: In Caribbean slang, especially in Jamaica, «mon» means "man" and is used to talk to a friend.
fact: In informal Scottish speech, «mon» can be a short form of «c'mon», which means "come on".
fact: In French, «mon» is a different word that means "my", as in «mon frère» (my brother). It is spelt the same but means something else.
exercise: In a school timetable, what does «Mon» stand for? | Moon | *Monday | Mountain | Monster
exercise: A friend says «Yeah, mon!» in a Caribbean story. What does mon mean here? | Monday | Come on, as a cheer | *"Man", a friendly word for a friend | My
exercise: A fan shouts «Mon the team!» at a football match. What does it mean? | *Come on, team! | Money for the team | My team | Monday team
test: In «Mon–Fri», which days are meant? | Monday to Sunday | *Monday to Friday | Monday only | Friday to Sunday | Friday to Monday
test: In a French sentence, «mon frère» means what? | our brother | your brother | his sister | *my brother
exam: A diary says «Mon: art club at 3pm». What does mon mean here? | Come on, as a cheer | My, before a masculine word | *Monday | Man, said to a friend
